{"_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "Vanessa and the Rude Customer", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "You Can Do It!", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 7, "type": "position"}, {"content": "scholar > Food for Thought > Dividing the Chicken", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 5, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.1", "type": "level"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Identify and provide solutions to problems in a range of social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations", "type": "secondary_8"}], "type": "objectives"}, {"content": "engenn6le05ob07re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Offering Advice and Solutions", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use some expressions such as \"would rather ('d rather)\" or \"might want to\" to express what someone wants or also to advice politely what to do in a particular situation.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": " Remember would rather + base form of a verb.<br><br> <span class=\"strong\">Correct</span>: I would rather have the vegan burger. <br><span class=\"strong\">Incorrect</span>: I would rather to have the vegan burger. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You're right. I'd rather have a free meal next time!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "You might want to resolve that issue quietly.", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Adverbs of Manner", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use adverbs of manner to describe how something is done.<br><span class=\"italic\">Example: She walked slowly.<br/>How did she walk? Slowly.</span>", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Many adverbs are formed by adding <span class=\"strong\">-ly</span> to an adjective:<br><span class=\"italic\">Examples: sad - sadly, curious - curiously</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You take out the letter -y and add <span class=\"strong\">-ily</span> to adjectives ending in -y.<br><span class=\"italic\">Example: angry - angrily</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The adjectives  <span class=\"strong\">fast</span>,  <span class=\"strong\">hard</span>,  <span class=\"strong\">well</span> and  <span class=\"strong\">straight</span> are exceptions.  They do not change when they become adverbs.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Adjective\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Adverb\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"nice<br/>\\t\\t\\tquiet<br/>angry<br/>harsh<br/>patient<br/>\\t\\t calm<br/>\\t\\t hard<br/>\\t\\tunusual\\t\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"nicely<br> quietly<br> angrily<br> harshly<br> patiently<br> calmly<br> hard<br> unusually\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "You handled that customer nicely. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "No one was shouting angrily yesterday. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Our chef works hard to keep that impression.", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "nicely", "type": "name"}, {"content": "in a pleasant manner ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adverb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You handled that customer nicely yesterday.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le05ob07aud01", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to describe how people work at a restaurant.", "type": "text"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"content": "angrily", "type": "name"}, {"content": "in an angry manner ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adverb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: No one was shouting angrily yesterday!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le05ob07aud02", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "quietly", "type": "name"}, {"content": "in a quiet manner ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": " (adverb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I'd rather resolve that issue quietly.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le05ob07aud03", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "intimidating ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "inspiring awe and fear", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Our chef knows that he is intimidating.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le05ob07aud04", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to get along", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to be on friendly terms with someone ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": " (verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I love it when everybody gets along.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le05ob07aud05", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "miscommunication ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "failure to communicate adequately ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I hope he doesn't write a complaint about our miscommunication problem.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le05ob07aud06", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "harsh", "type": "name"}, {"content": "rough; severe ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": " (adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I hope we won't get a harsh review!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le05ob07aud07", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Think of your favorite character (from a book, a movie \u2026 )", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Describe the character's behavior. How does he or she behave?", "type": "text"}, {"content": "What happens in the story? How does it happen?", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Use 6 clues. Remember to use adverbs of manner.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Try to guess your partner's character!", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"content": "I talk about how things happen.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I talk about how someone behaves.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I play a game with my partner.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "contents": [{}], "_data": [], "id": 0, "type": "welcome"}, {"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "title": "", "type": "audio", "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"image": "engenn6le05ob07re2img07.jpg", "time": "0", "id": 0, "text": ""}, {"image": "engenn6le05ob07re2img07.jpg", "time": "100", "id": 1, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Good job today, Sarah. You handled that vegetarian customer nicely. <br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sarah</span>: Thanks! I exaggerated our chef's persona a little. I hope he won't mind.<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>:\tOh, don't worry about that! Our chef knows he is intimidating and he works hard to keep that impression. Anyway, I liked how you patiently went through the menu with our clients yesterday. I also noticed that you dealt with unusual requests calmly."}, {"image": "engenn6le05ob07re2img01.jpg", "time": "25700", "id": 2, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Sarah</span>: It also helped that no one was shouting angrily yesterday! <br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: That's true. I love it when everybody gets along. It makes my job as a manager much easier.  <br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sarah</span>: By the way, what about that angry customer the other day?  <br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: I invited him to come back for a free meal. I'd rather resolve the issue quietly before he writes a complaint about our miscommunication problem."}, {"image": "engenn6le05ob07re2img07.jpg", "time": "47500", "id": 3, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Sarah</span>: Do you think he would do that? <br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Yes, sadly. We might want to have a look at the paper soon. Something tells me we're in for a harsh review."}], "audiosrc": "engenn6le05ob07re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn6le05ob07re2img07.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "id": 1}], "exercises": [{"templat